    "Freeholder",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 18 of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, as amended.",
    "The development hereby approved shall be constructed in accordance with the materials stipulated on drawings 13/RR-06 R1, 13/RR-07 R2, 13/RR-09 R2, 13/RR-10 R0, WoodyMan Ltd technical quote for Ms Laura Ball at 13 Rosebery Road, Existing Property and Streetscene Photographs supporting document and thereafter maintained and retained unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason:  To safeguard the visual amenities of the conservation area and to ensure compliance with Policies 28 and 30 of the Local Plan 2018.",
    "The first floor flank windows in the northern elevation of the development hereby approved shall be glazed with obscure glass and fixed shut to a height of 1.7 metres above the finished floor level of the room in which the window is installed in a manner that they cannot be opened and retained thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the current level of privacy enjoyed by the occupants of adjoining properties in accordance with and to ensure compliance with the Sutton Local Plan 2018.\r",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Reasonable Exception Statement - Fire Safety at 13 Rosebery Road, Cheam SM1 2BW and dated 21.08.2026.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12."
